mar" color="green">verb</font></div><div>estar de acuerdo con</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>be fit<div>servir</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>able to expect<div>caérsele el pelo</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>arrive late<div>llegar tarde</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>be similar to something<div>ser como</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>do as you wish<ol><li><div>adelante</div></li><li><div>con confianza</div></li><li><div>sírvase</div></li><li><div>sírvete</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>go away; get out<ol><li><div>esfumarse</div></li><li><div>largarse</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to be responsible for<div>ser responsabilidad de</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><ol><li><div>estar atento</div></li><li><div>estar pendiente</div></li><li><div>estarse atento</div></li><li><div>estarse pendiente</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to have gained an insight that could lead to future success<ol><li><div>calar</div></li><li><div>sospechar</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to be free of or released from a troublesome or undesirable person or object<ol><li><div>desfacerse de</div></li><li><div>deshacerse de</div></li><li><div>librarse de</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>be correct in one's judgement or statement about something<ol><li><div>tener razón</div></li><li><div>estar en lo correcto</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">biː ɹaɪt bæk</font>/<br>
